 named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** BUG-260916-20xt79\n- **Title:** BUG-260916-20xt79: fix-nwerror-wifiaware-xcode16-sdk-compatibility\n- **Parent:** STORY-260916-2d5zk1\n\n### Description\n\nHosted run 35048178384 for PR6 head a46e2ba351a81e42f2907805b4cda2c313af7bd1 fails compiling MacOSSSHBootstrapErrorMapper.swift:37: NWError has no member wifiAware on Xcode 16.4 / Swift 6.1 / macOS SDK 15.5. The defect predates the last Sendable fix. Implement the smallest SDK-compatible error mapping correction, retain privacy-safe categories, validate applicable tests and prepare an independently reviewable delta. This task owns the new product correction; it must not require full PR6 landing or unrelated CI fixes for handoff.\n\n### Scope\n\nMacOSSSHBootstrapErrorMapper and directly relevant compatibility tests/documentation only. No VPN operations, routes, tooling edits, gate relaxation, unrelated fixes or publication before independent review.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nDeclared older SDK compiles the mapper; current SDK retains intended error mapping and safe fallback behavior; focused checks pass and evidence distinguishes local toolchain from hosted proof; independent reviewer accepts exact candidate before composition into PR6.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### BUG-260916-20xt79_implementation-brief.md\n> Narrow SDK compatibility repair and handoff contract\n\nImplement only the wifiAware SDK-compatibility bug. Muse Spark 1.3 contributor max is the authorized implementation model. macOS is the target; iOS deferred. Evidence: control-root .task-board/.resources/TASK-260908-34gi0y/TASK-260908-34gi0y_ci-35048178384-failed-job.log and TASK-260908-34gi0y_results.md. The mapper blob 5b47bd80 is identical on protected main b3422b0 and PR6 a46e2ba. Work from the freshly verified protected-main managed workspace; do not move root main or managed refs manually. Diagnose the smallest compatibility fix and add only meaningful focused validation. Report toolchain and SDK differences honestly; full PR6 green/landing is a later delivery task, not this producer handoff gate. Do not change tooling, install anything, use real VPN, configure routes, expand scope, or commit on managed Story branches. Preserve human Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com> signing identity/key /Users/iv/.ssh/ivanopcode; ordinary timestamps. Preserve all foreign changes/evidence. Stop at independent review with an exact candidate; no publication or landing yet. If supported provisioning or handoff refuses due to external dependency or incompatible scope, attach a precise evidence packet and route blocked rather than retry unchanged conditions or falsify a checklist. Read independent recovery audit TASK-260916-p5tbh8 only if needed. Parent owns subsequent Astra-low review and composition into PR6. Operational config is /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resume-20260916/task-board.config.json; never fall back to stale root config.\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `BUG-260916-20xt79_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(BUG-260916-20xt79, name=BUG-260916-20xt79_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff BUG-260916-20xt79 --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260916-2d5zk1.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260916-2d5zk1/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260916-2d5zk1`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n"}}
